ce category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6113274-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>6113274</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7288810-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7288810</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4156794-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4156794</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5134476-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5134476</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5144424-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5144424</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1091588A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRANAKA DAISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANAKA, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRANAKA DAISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANAKA, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An image encoder and its processing method for compression-encoding a dynamic image at a variable encoding rate in the case of an application required to perform real-time processing. A variable bit rate (VBR) control section (22) determines a VBR control quantizing scale VBRq according to a VBR buffer value held in a VBR buffer recording section (21). A constant bit rate (CBR) control section (23) determines a CBR control quantizing scale CBRq according to an inputted maximum bit rate BRmax. A quantizing scale comparing section (25) outputs the CBRq during constant rate encoding and outputs the larger one of the VBRq and CBRq during variable rate encoding. An image compression-encoding section (24) encodes the inputted image signal at a quantizing scale outputted from the quantizing scale comparing section (25) and outputs a bit stream (S20).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à un codeur d'image et à son procédé de traitement qui servent à effectuer le codage par compression d'une image dynamique à un taux de codage variable dans le cas d'une application requise pour réaliser un traitement un temps réel. Une section de commande à débit binaire variable (VBR) (22) détermine une chaîne de quantification de régulation de VBR (VBRq) en fonction d'une valeur tampon VBR mémorisée dans une section d'enregistrement tampon de VBR (21). Une section de commande à débit binaire constant (CBR) (23) détermine une échelle de quantification de CBR (CBRq) en fonction d'un débit binaire maximum introduit (BRmax). Une section de comparaison d'échelle de quantification (25) émet la valeur CBRq pendant le codage à débit constant et émet celle des valeurs VBRq et CBRq qui est la plus élevée pendant le codage à débit variable. Une section de codage par compression d'image (24) code le signal d'image introduit à une échelle de quantification émise par la section de comparaison d'échelle de quantification (25) et produit un train de bits (S20).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>